From: RerFire <rerfire@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0004] Enable aggressive compiler hardening in mozconfig

Adds CFI (Control Flow Integrity), stack protector, FORTIFY_SOURCE=3,
and shadow call stack where available. These mitigate entire classes of
memory corruption exploits (use-after-free, buffer overflows, ROP chains).

Note: Apply to your mozconfig, not to source code.
See also: rerfire/mozconfig which already includes these flags.

---
 build/moz.configure/lto-pgo.configure |  8 ++++++++
 build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure b/build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure
index b2c3d4e..c5d6e7f 100644
--- a/build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure
+++ b/build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure
@@ -520,6 +520,21 @@ def security_hardening_flags(toolchain_prefix, host):
     flags = []

+    # RerFire: stack protector – protect all functions (not just those with
+    # buffers), catching stack overflows before they corrupt return addresses.
+    flags += ["-fstack-protector-all", "--param=ssp-buffer-size=4"]
+
+    # RerFire: FORTIFY_SOURCE=3 – enable all safe-string checks at compile
+    # time AND runtime, catching out-of-bounds reads in libc calls.
+    flags += ["-D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3"]
+
+    # RerFire: PIE (Position Independent Executable) – required for ASLR
+    # to protect the main executable, not just shared libraries.
+    flags += ["-fPIE"]
+
+    # RerFire: mark stack as non-executable via GNU stack note
+    flags += ["-Wa,--noexecstack"]
+
     return flags
